**Anserini reproductions from document collection**

+ **Models**: [BGE-large-en-v1.5](https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5) with flat indexes (using ONNX for on-the-fly query encoding)
+ **Config**: [`${yaml_short}`](${yaml})
+ **Template**: [`${template_short}`](${template})

This page describes reproductions from the raw document collection using [BGE-large-en-v1.5](https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5) on [BRIGHT &mdash; Earth Science](https://brightbenchmark.github.io/).
See the following paper for more details:

> Shitao Xiao, Zheng Liu, Peitian Zhang, and Niklas Muennighoff. [C-Pack: Packaged Resources To Advance General Chinese Embedding.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.07597) _arXiv:2309.07597_, 2023.

In these experiments, we are using ONNX to perform query encoding on the fly.

This page is automatically generated from [this template](${template}) by the `GenerateReproductionDocsFromDocumentCollectionTest` JUnit test case, so do not modify this page directly; modify the template instead.

From one of our Waterloo servers (e.g., `orca`), the following command will perform the complete reproduction, end to end:

```bash
bin/run.sh io.anserini.reproduce.ReproduceFromDocumentCollection --index --verify --search --config ${test_name}
```

All the BRIGHT corpora, encoded by the BGE-large-en-v1.5 model, are available for download:

```bash
wget https://huggingface.co/datasets/castorini/collections-bright/resolve/main/bright-bge-large-en-v1.5.tar -P collections/
tar xvf collections/bright-bge-large-en-v1.5.tar -C collections/
```

The tarball is 13 GB and has MD5 checksum `0ce2634d34d3d467cd1afd74f2f63c7b`.
After download and unpacking the corpora, the `ReproduceFromDocumentCollection` command above should work without any issue.

